The class ReplicationManager is internal sealed, so we cannot subclass or access it directly from outside the assembly. The logger is a private field, so we cannot inject a mock logger easily.

Since the apply_refactor tool is not available, and we cannot change the production code, the best approach is to write a test class inside the same namespace Garnet.cluster and use InternalsVisibleTo attribute if it exists to access internal types. If not, we can use reflection to set the private logger field to a mock ILogger.

I will write a test class in the Garnet.cluster namespace that uses reflection to set the private logger field to a mock ILogger, then call ProcessPrimaryStream with conditions that cause the logger.LogError call on line 49 (when clusterProvider.replicationManager.CannotStreamAOF is true).

I will submit this test now.

